{"kind":"request","text":"The desktop AI app runs two server processes, and a card loses its view\n\nScope: J2's acceptance, 2082efd9. Hugh ran the steps at about 12:17 EST, on the domain fix. The card's frame now opens, so the domain was a real fault. The card shows \"This view is no longer retained. Open it again; this call sent no act.\" The tool's own response, as the app shows it, reads \"change: ready; manifest 39, revision 1. 1 item.\"\n\nThe cause, from reading and not yet shown by a run: the app starts every local server twice. Processes 7707 and 7727 both run `apps/views/src/node.ts`, started one second apart under one parent, and each session since 11:06 shows such a pair in `~/Library/Logs/Claude/mcp-server-dap-views.log`. The model's `view_change` opens the view in one process. The card's tool call reaches the other. `ViewSessions` holds views in the memory of one process (`#instances`, `packages/mcp/src/views/session.ts:155`), so the second process finds no instance and throws at line 177. The log fits: `tools/call` id 5 at 17:17:10.429 answered in 1 ms, which no network read could do, and that log file shows no call that opened the view. It also explains why the 11:07 session logged no `tools/call`.\n\nDo this:\n1. Show it first: a test with two `node.ts` processes on one home, where one opens a view and the other answers the card's call. It fails today by this message.\n2. Make a card work when its calls reach another process of the same home. You choose how. Weigh a process that reopens the view from what the card can send, against view state on disk under the home. Name what each costs for held reads, for pending acts, and for a signed act that must not go twice. An act's custody must stay one record across both processes, so read how custody behaves under two processes now and say so.\n3. Run the path under the two-process shape, and cite the card workflow's run.\n4. Move the person's steps to that head, and tell me.\n\nThis is the app's normal shape, so every person on the desktop app meets it, on every view. Treat the card's message itself as a defect too: \"Open it again\" does not help a person whose every call reaches the other process.\n\nThe three console lines \"Unrecognized Content-Security-Policy directive 'webrtc'\" are not ours by a search of `packages/mcp` and `apps/views`. Hugh reports them, and the card still loaded. Note them and do not chase them, unless the next session shows they matter.\n\nOrder: first.","body":{"conditions":"A card works when its calls reach a second server process of the same home, under a two-process test and a control, approved by the checker and landed on main, with the person's steps moved to that head.","target_head":"89e59c128084f9c51b20747a72b3f32b050cf097","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}